released almost 20 years ago jeepers  creepers is a classic horror movie and  it's even spawned two sequels  like any good scary film it can still  induce hair-raising fear  years later so here's a recap on what  makes it one of a kind  jeepers creepers follow siblings darius  gary jenner and patricia trish jenner  who begin the movie on a road trip home  from college  they're on spring break in rural florida  on a country highway  with time on their hands and taking the  scenic route to where they're going so  the scary movie setup is  perfect unfortunately for darry and  trish they don't take the quicker way  home  which means they cross paths with a  mysterious demonic creature  before they know it a rusty ominous  looking truck starts tailgating darry  and trish  it's a subtle nod to another ominous  truck that made its appearance in the  1971 steven spielberg directed tv movie  duel  in that movie star dennis weaver was in  the sights of an  unseen driver behind the wheel of a  massive dangerous peterbilt 281  in the case of jeepers creepers the  audience finds out pretty quickly that  the driver of this truck  is a strange creature called the creeper  he's not human and he can fly  fast which we find out after tris starts  questioning his movements  wondering how someone can loot their car  and get back and forth to the church  where the creeper keeps his victims in  such record time trish eventually takes  a guess  maybe he can leap to all buildings in a  single bound yes the creeper can fly  unlike many movie monsters though the  creeper doesn't just come out at night  he not only drives but also appears to  do his business during all hours of the  day  darry and trish first see the creeper  dumping bodies at the abandoned  church that's conveniently located in  plain view of the road  not only do they see this strange figure  unloading corpses into a large pipe that  sticks out of the ground  but they get a clear full frontal shot  of the creeper after he spots them  watching him  in most monster movies the monster  doesn't usually fight on equal terms  monsters stick to their strengths  vampires for example do their monster  mashing at night  and for obvious reasons as sunlight is  one of their biggest weaknesses  however the creeper doesn't have that  limitation he isn't afraid to roam free  and wreak havoc during the daytime  after the creeper sees darry and trish  watching him he proceeds to get in his  truck and chase after them  he rams into their car several times  until their vehicle goes off the side of  the road  and then he speeds off into the distance  at this point in the movie  the creeper is only trying to scare the  siblings so they could have presumably  gone on their way  mostly unscathed but darry decides to be  a hero  darry convinces his sister to go back to  the church to see what the creeper is  throwing down the pipe  after all bloodstained sheets that are  shaped like human bodies could be  anything right  wrapped in a sheet wrapped and roped in  a sheet  wrapped and roped in a sheet with red  stains on it  darry hears something coming from the  pipe so he has his sister hold his feet  as he tries to get a better view of what  lurks below  he sees rats and freaks out trish lets  go of his legs and he falls into the  pipe  finding an underground tomb filled with  bodies and one poor victim who's still  barely alive but on his way out i found  our body  what i found  it's the creepers hideout also referred  to as the house of pain  instead of helping darry find a way out  trish does as he orders and leaves him  to fend for himself so she can try to  flag down a passing car  but against all odds darry makes it out  their car starts  and they drive away even at this point  darry and trish could probably have left  this freaky town and called for help  once they were out of harm's way  but darry of course wants justice for  the lifeless victims he's found  so they go to a nearby diner to contact  the authorities  this unfortunately gives the creeper  more time to find out that someone  discovered his lair  with all signs pointing to darry and  trish it also leaves the door open for  the creeper to discover that darry and  trish are in possession  of something he needs after finding the  bodies and linking them to the creeper  the siblings contact local authorities  to solve a case involving hundreds of  dead people  stuck up on the walls like some psycho  version of the sistine chapel  as they get in deeper darry and trish  actually take pretty logical steps to  deal with the monster  and that's saying something for a horror  movie a genre that routinely sees the  characters do the exact opposite of what  they should do  even after the first cops to respond or  killed by the creeper the siblings drive  to an old woman's house and asked to  call the police  caught in the crosshairs the creeper  kills the woman escaping to their  vehicle  darry and trish momentarily hurt the  creeper by running him over  by now they've seen this inhuman face  and know he can fly  so it wouldn't have been out of the  ordinary for them to stop seeking help  from the authorities  in typical horror movie logic dick takes  here that darry and trish go rogue  without consulting the police anymore  thinking that no one else would believe  their tail i'm being chased by a guy who  likes to  pull tongues on his severed heads with  his teeth special extension for that  but instead they doggedly press on and  go to a police station  trying again to alert local law  enforcement this inadvertently involves  them in hearing about what a lady sees  in her psychic dreams  darry and trish first find out what the  creeper is because of a random phone  call  while they're in the diner an unknown  woman calls them on a payphone that  happens to be right next to them  the woman somehow knows who they are and  the danger that lies ahead  she tells them that if they hear the  song jeepers creepers they need to run  away as fast as possible  only after they arrive at the police  station does the audience discover who  the woman is  a psychic named giselle gay hartman  giselle tells them that the creature is  an  ancient being that awakens every 23rd  spring for 23 days to feast on the  living  the creeper eats human body parts that  then become part of him  finding his victims by smelling their  fear there's something he can  smell something that tells it if there's  anything inside someone that it might  like and he's found something he wants  from trish and dary  the creeper not only cannibalizes  victims but is also  virtually impossible to kill case in  point trish runs over the creeper  multiple times with a car  you think he's dead they never are  the creeper momentarily appears  mutilated and dead but then a wing  sprouts up from the creeper and the  siblings drive off in fear  they have no clue what they're dealing  with but they're not going to stick  around to find out  the creeper follows trish and dary to  the police station and rejuvenates  himself by eating prisoners body parts  so while the creeper can be hurt at  least in his first film in the series he  can't be killed  that makes jeepers creepers even more  terrifying  since the only way to defeat the creeper  is to survive his 23 days of terror  darry never stood a chance the movie  takes its name from the 1938 song  jeepers creepers but the song itself  isn't just the title of the movie  it also plays a significant sinister  role in the story  after giselle plays it for darry and  trish on the phone she gives them an  ominous warning to run whenever it's  played  they hear it again in their car then  gisele sings it at the police station  jeepers creepers where'd you get those  people perhaps most maddening of all the  song plays at the end of the movie  during the big reveal  since the creeper is attracted to  specific humans and will stop at nothing  until he gets what he desires  the song's lyrics are decidedly sadistic  when paired with jeepers creepers the  movie  the lyrics in fact foreshadow darry's  fate  jeepers creepers has a memorable ending  easily forgotten over time  and unfortunately only one of the two  main characters survive  trish in a last-ditch effort to save her  brother tries sacrificing herself  telling the creeper to take her instead  because she's stronger  the creeper contemplates her offer but  then flies off into the night with dary  trish lives on to tell her story but  darry perishes at the end of jeepers  creepers in a brutal death  darry isn't shown again until the  graphic ending in which his eyes are  missing  the creeper as if he's posing for the  camera stands on the other side of darry  and  looks through the holes in darry's face  the creeper's eyes have presumably been  replaced with darys  disturbingly making darry's eyes appear  to look through the holes of where they  once were  not only does the creeper survive the  first installment it ends on an  outright sinister note with no hope in  sight a defeated and emotionally drained  trish leaves the police station  not knowing if she'll ever see her  brother again it's fair to assume that  she knows she's already lost him  as there's no way of finding the creeper  and he can't be killed  and of course the final scene of the  movie features the creeper still alive  and peacefully working in his new lair  now with darry's eyes and his own head  it's no wonder jeepers creepers haunts  people's dreams to this day this isn't a  movie you forget because of how  long ago it came out more like a movie  you forget because the ending is the  stuff of nightmares  and you choose not to remember check out  one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

